WEBVTT


00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:02.260
You are looking at a living,

00:00:02.261 --> 00:00:06.601
breathing, interactive ecosystem that I built for my AI agents

00:00:06.620 --> 00:00:08.900
so that I could gamify my entire life

00:00:08.901 --> 00:00:10.561
and all my businesses and everything.

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:13.420
And within this little ecosystem,

00:00:13.421 --> 00:00:17.241
we built these two factory rooms that run autonomous businesses.

00:00:17.420 --> 00:00:21.440
And the first autonomous business we started was an Etsy store.

00:00:21.441 --> 00:00:24.261
On this conveyor belt here is a representation of that Etsy store.

00:00:24.262 --> 00:00:27.421
We could actually access the Etsy store and see how much we've made

00:00:27.422 --> 00:00:30.361
and manage the store from this little dashboard here.

00:00:30.420 --> 00:00:34.420
And yes, we have about 40 orders on the Etsy store so far.

00:00:34.421 --> 00:00:36.461
We're just about to hit $2,000 in revenue.

00:00:36.462 --> 00:00:39.701
And the biggest question I've been asked has been about the Etsy store

00:00:39.702 --> 00:00:43.081
actually. And I want to go over how you guys at home

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:45.880
can build your own autonomous Etsy store that runs

00:00:46.340 --> 00:00:48.640
entirely on its own with your AI agents.

00:00:48.700 --> 00:00:52.260
So what you're gonna need first is AI agents.

00:00:52.261 --> 00:00:53.461
You're gonna need about three.

00:00:53.462 --> 00:00:56.601
I recommend at least having about three AI agents.

00:00:57.340 --> 00:00:59.740
So let me start from step 1,

00:00:59.741 --> 00:01:02.381
research agent. This is Nova.

00:01:02.382 --> 00:01:05.201
Nova hangs out in his little research lab

00:01:05.319 --> 00:01:08.260
and all he does is throughout the day,

00:01:08.261 --> 00:01:10.301
he'll do research on Etsy,

00:01:10.302 --> 00:01:12.741
on products that are performing well on Etsy,

00:01:12.742 --> 00:01:14.941
on stores that are performing well on Etsy

00:01:14.942 --> 00:01:17.781
and how we can take inspiration from those stores

00:01:17.782 --> 00:01:20.281
and apply it to our own Etsy store. Right?

00:01:20.380 --> 00:01:24.760
So he'll take that research and he'll Bring it over to forge over here

00:01:25.620 --> 00:01:33.640
and forge has access to Printify and Nano Banana Pro.

00:01:33.720 --> 00:01:36.700
So you're gonna need Nano Banana Pro which is Google,

00:01:36.701 --> 00:01:39.781
which is Gemini which will cost you about $20 a month.

00:01:39.782 --> 00:01:44.361
This gives your agent access to actually design products.

00:01:44.660 --> 00:01:48.380
So that is step one step two is actually gonna be an Etsy store.

00:01:48.381 --> 00:01:52.801
This will cost you about $30 to start a seller account on Etsy

00:01:53.140 --> 00:01:56.480
and you're gonna need a Printify account.

00:01:56.660 --> 00:02:00.680
Printify has all of these products right here

00:02:01.060 --> 00:02:05.300
and you can have your agent slap your

00:02:05.301 --> 00:02:10.141
or the designs it creates on these templates here

00:02:10.142 --> 00:02:12.021
in which Printify will actually

00:02:12.022 --> 00:02:14.421
when you get an order on your Etsy store

00:02:14.422 --> 00:02:16.381
will print your design on

00:02:16.382 --> 00:02:21.201
that your AI agent made and ship it out to your customer for you right?

00:02:21.500 --> 00:02:25.880
And all you have to do is connect your Printify API key to your agent,

00:02:25.900 --> 00:02:28.820
connect your Etsy API key to your agent

00:02:28.821 --> 00:02:30.681
to your main factory agent

00:02:30.780 --> 00:02:34.740
and then that is essentially all it needs to start creating products

00:02:34.980 --> 00:02:40.260
So Etsy Printify and then Gemini Nano Banana Pro to create the designs

00:02:40.261 --> 00:02:43.461
right? And then you're probably asking what is the third agent?

00:02:43.462 --> 00:02:45.021
Do you have research agent?

00:02:45.022 --> 00:02:48.841
You have the agent that makes the designs and puts it on Etsy

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:51.380
over here we have the media agent

00:02:51.381 --> 00:02:53.421
which pumps out TikToks all day

00:02:53.422 --> 00:02:56.681
and actually helps me with my YouTube channel and stuff like that

00:02:56.860 --> 00:03:02.540
but forge Will create the product photos from these templates

00:03:02.541 --> 00:03:04.561
and he'll take these template photos.

00:03:04.940 --> 00:03:07.100
Not exactly these. Usually they're like the empty,

00:03:07.101 --> 00:03:08.421
like there's no model on them.

00:03:08.422 --> 00:03:13.181
Usually he takes like we take these usually so that it looks clean,

00:03:13.182 --> 00:03:13.741
right?

00:03:13.742 --> 00:03:18.621
And he'll take these product photos he creates and give them to Pixel

00:03:18.622 --> 00:03:22.801
and Pixel will actually curate slideshows and post it on TikTok.

00:03:23.440 --> 00:03:28.380
So that is essentially all you need to have an entirely

00:03:28.381 --> 00:03:32.541
autonomous Etsy store. The only thing I would recommend other than that

00:03:32.542 --> 00:03:34.661
is to create this system here,

00:03:34.662 --> 00:03:36.661
which I created when I first started the Etsy store.

00:03:36.662 --> 00:03:38.201
I don't really use this anymore,

00:03:38.260 --> 00:03:42.340
but forge, when he started designing in his early career,

00:03:42.341 --> 00:03:45.701
he was trash. His designs looked terrible.

00:03:45.702 --> 00:03:47.941
So what I did is I built this system,

00:03:47.942 --> 00:03:49.501
this approval reject system,

00:03:49.502 --> 00:03:52.921
a feedback system. So he would show me a design.

00:03:53.100 --> 00:03:54.780
I would either say approve,

00:03:54.781 --> 00:03:57.481
I like it or reject. This shit is garbage.

00:03:57.540 --> 00:03:59.660
And I did this a few hundred times with him.

00:03:59.661 --> 00:04:01.281
It took about two or three days.

00:04:01.300 --> 00:04:01.980
And now

00:04:01.981 --> 00:04:05.181
he's at the point where I completely trust him to make products.

00:04:05.182 --> 00:04:08.341
His products are great. So that's what I would recommend doing

00:04:08.342 --> 00:04:11.681
is definitely setting up some sort of system at first

00:04:11.700 --> 00:04:17.300
so that you can train your agent to actually produce what you want.

00:04:17.301 --> 00:04:19.530
And yeah, that's how you start up your own Etsy store.
